<div>
	<div>
		<p> <u><b> Oral reading</b></u> </p>
	</div>
	<div>
		<p>
			<b> Purpose: </b> The oral evaluation determines how Jane reads and understands materials at home and school
		</p>
	</div>
	<div>
		<p>
			<b>  Administration: </b> We asked Jane to read 3 passages aloud, one each at the 2, 3, and 4 grade levels. After Jane finished reading a passage, we
			asked Jane questions about that passage to measure Jane's comprehension.
		</p>
	</div>
	<div>
		<p>
			While Jane read orally, we counted the number of miscues Jane made.
		</p>
		<p>
			<i>(A miscue is a mistake or interruption in reading. When Jane experiences miscues, Jane's fluency suffers; and sometimes Jane's comprehension is affected.)</i>
		</p>
	</div>
</div>